    - id: governance
      markdown: "# Governance & handoff\n\nMake responsibilities and next steps explicit.\n\n## RACI responsibilities\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.1 -->\n| Activity | Responsible | Accountable | Consulted | Informed |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Approve specification baseline | Tech lead | Customer Experience director | Security architect | Support Operations |\n| Release to production | Platform Engineering | Tech lead | Support Operations | Customers |\n| Operate on-call | Platform Engineering | Platform Engineering lead | Support Operations | Customer Experience |\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Reviewers and approvals\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.2 -->\nSecurity section: security architect. Operations: platform lead. Baseline approval: Customer Experience director and tech lead.\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Milestones and dependencies\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.3 -->\nPilot (June 15): REQ-001 to REQ-004 and REQ-006; depends on the OIDC client. General availability (August 1): all requirements.\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Readiness and unresolved decisions\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.4 -->\nEmail provider (SES or Postmark) — owner: tech lead — by week 2 — blocks REQ-005 only.\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Contributor onboarding\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.5 -->\nRead .plan/README.md and the conventions; run the Docker setup in under 30 minutes; first task tagged “good first issue”.\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Implementation tasks\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.6 -->\nTASK-01 Request submission API (REQ-001, TEST-001). TASK-02 Organization isolation (REQ-002, TEST-002). TASK-03 Timeline and replies (REQ-003, REQ-004, TEST-003).\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Coding-agent instructions\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.7 -->\nAlways run pnpm lint and pnpm test before finishing; keep REQ/ADR identifiers; update .plan records. Never weaken organization isolation, never edit an approved baseline, and never guess an open decision — report it.\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Project license\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.8 -->\nProprietary (all rights reserved)\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Distribution model\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.9 -->\nHosted service (SaaS)\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Allowed dependency licenses\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.10 -->\n- Permissive (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, ISC)\n- Weak copyleft (LGPL, MPL, EPL)\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## License compliance in the pipeline\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.11 -->\nYes\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Specification persistence model\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.12 -->\nLiving specification (kept in sync, drift checked)\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n\n## Large feature decomposition\n\n<!-- sdd:answer governance.13 -->\nOne specification per epic or release\n<!-- sdd:end -->\n"
      diagram: "gantt\n  title Delivery milestones\n  dateFormat YYYY-MM-DD\n  section Specification\n  Baseline approved :done, spec, 2026-01-05, 14d\n  section Build\n  Pilot release :pilot, after spec, 45d\n  General availability :milestone, ga, after pilot, 0d"
      answers:
        governance.1:
          value: "[[\"Approve specification baseline\",\"Tech lead\",\"Customer Experience director\",\"Security architect\",\"Support Operations\"],[\"Release to production\",\"Platform Engineering\",\"Tech lead\",\"Support Operations\",\"Customers\"],[\"Operate on-call\",\"Platform Engineering\",\"Platform Engineering lead\",\"Support Operations\",\"Customer Experience\"]]"
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.2:
          value: "Security section: security architect. Operations: platform lead. Baseline approval: Customer Experience director and tech lead."
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.3:
          value: "Pilot (June 15): REQ-001 to REQ-004 and REQ-006; depends on the OIDC client. General availability (August 1): all requirements."
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.4:
          value: "Email provider (SES or Postmark) — owner: tech lead — by week 2 — blocks REQ-005 only."
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.5:
          value: Read .plan/README.md and the conventions; run the Docker setup in under 30 minutes; first task tagged “good first issue”.
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.6:
          value: "TASK-01 Request submission API (REQ-001, TEST-001). TASK-02 Organization isolation (REQ-002, TEST-002). TASK-03 Timeline and replies (REQ-003, REQ-004, TEST-003)."
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.7:
          value: "Always run pnpm lint and pnpm test before finishing; keep REQ/ADR identifiers; update .plan records. Never weaken organization isolation, never edit an approved baseline, and never guess an open decision — report it."
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.8:
          value: Proprietary (all rights reserved)
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.9:
          value: Hosted service (SaaS)
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.10:
          value: "[\"Permissive (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, ISC)\",\"Weak copyleft (LGPL, MPL, EPL)\"]"
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.11:
          value: yes
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.12:
          value: "Living specification (kept in sync, drift checked)"
          state: answered
          reason: ""
        governance.13:
          value: One specification per epic or release
          state: answered
